WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:05.143
In this lesson we'll write the page for a component from scratch,

00:05.443 --> 00:11.657
and talk about why the order of the sections matters more than the sections themselves.

01:12.500 --> 01:15.571
Most teams start with the properties table,

01:15.871 --> 01:19.371
because that is what the code gives you for free.

01:19.671 --> 01:22.886
But nobody opens the docs to learn the props;

01:23.186 --> 01:27.686
they open them to find out whether this is the right component.

03:40.500 --> 03:43.786
So the first section is usage: what it is for,

03:44.086 --> 03:47.014
what it is not for, and the alternatives.

03:47.314 --> 03:50.243
Two real examples beat ten abstract ones.

06:05.500 --> 06:08.000
Next, the anatomy.

06:08.300 --> 06:10.800
Name every part.

06:11.100 --> 06:14.600
The names end up in the code, in the design file,

06:14.900 --> 06:18.757
and in conversations, so pick them once and keep them.

08:50.500 --> 08:53.929
And then the properties, with every state shown.

08:54.229 --> 08:58.157
A state without an example is a state nobody will test.
